# Implementation Plan - Sliding Panel Auth Redesign

The goal is to implement a professional "Sliding Panel" transition for the login/register flow. This design uses a fixed-size card container where an overlay panel slides horizontally to reveal the appropriate form, creating a high-end, tactile interface.

## Proposed Changes

### [Auth Components]

#### [MODIFY] [AuthContainer.tsx](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/proyecto%20informatico_1%20frontend/Proyecto_Informatico/src/components/auth/AuthContainer.tsx)
- **Container Structure**: Implement a fixed-size card (e.g., `max-w-4xl`, `h-[600px]`) with `relative` and `overflow-hidden`.
- **Sliding Overlay**: 
    - Create an "Overlay Container" that occupies 50% of the card width.
    - Use Framer Motion to slide this overlay between `x: 0` (Login state, revealing form on right) and `x: 100%` (Register state, revealing form on left).
    - Inside the overlay, place the [DevTips](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/proyecto%20informatico_1%20frontend/Proyecto_Informatico/src/components/auth/DevTips.tsx#25-84) and a "Switch" button.
- **Form Reveal**: Place the Login and Register forms *behind* the overlay, positioned absolutely so they are revealed as the overlay slides away.

#### [MODIFY] [AuthCard.tsx](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/proyecto%20informatico_1%20frontend/Proyecto_Informatico/src/components/auth/AuthCard.tsx)
- Remove the internal `AnimatePresence` toggle.
- Instead, export two separate sub-components (or use props) to render the Login and Register forms side-by-side or in fixed positions that align with the [AuthContainer](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/proyecto%20informatico_1%20frontend/Proyecto_Informatico/src/components/auth/AuthContainer.tsx#12-155)'s sliding logic.
- Ensure perfect vertical/horizontal centering for each form.

#### [MODIFY] [DevTips.tsx](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/proyecto%20informatico_1%20frontend/Proyecto_Informatico/src/components/auth/DevTips.tsx)
- Adjust the layout to be more compact to fit inside the 50% overlay panel.
- Ensure the color contrast is high against the shifting background.

## Verification Plan

### Manual Verification
- **Toggle Transition**: Click "Register" and verify the overlay slides smoothly to the right, revealing the signup form.
- **Toggle Back**: Click "Login" and verify the overlay slides back to the left, revealing the login form.
- **Centering**: Confirm all inputs and buttons are perfectly centered and fully visible within the fixed-size card.
- **Blobs**: Ensure background blobs move *behind* the card or are integrated into the card for depth.
